WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.100
Why does this chapter come with
so many questions up front?

2
00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:08.337
Because an agent works at machine speed,
so whatever it can reach, it reaches fast.

3
00:00:08.337 --> 00:00:10.851
Microsoft's answer is Agent ID.

4
00:00:10.851 --> 00:00:14.784
A blueprint holds the credentials
and creates the agent identities,

5
00:00:14.784 --> 00:00:17.613
which hold the permissions
and show up in the logs.

6
00:00:17.613 --> 00:00:22.517
That structure has a sharp edge: the
blueprint gets tokens on behalf of every

7
00:00:22.517 --> 00:00:27.576
agent under it, so one compromised
blueprint credential is every agent at once.

8
00:00:27.576 --> 00:00:31.217
The platform became
generally available in April;

9
00:00:31.217 --> 00:00:34.390
the extra security
features need Agent 365.
